<<<
clench, -inch. The spellings are so far differentiated as to be generally applied thus: we clench a nail, a rivet, our hands, jaws, & teeth, an object held, a rope; we clinch an argument & a bargain, & the fact or statement that settles an argument is a clincher.
===
**clench, -inch.** The spellings are so far differentiated as to be generally applied thus: we *clench* a nail, a rivet, our hands, jaws, & teeth, an object held, a rope; we *clinch* an argument & a bargain, & the fact or statement that settles an argument is a *clincher*.
>>>

